# oh105, the carter who knows your gran (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle oh105
revision 1
state ready
dialect oakhaven
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_tristram_rainridge
written_by claude
title the carter who knows your gran
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk has_opinions_about_everyone_s_grandmother
likes plum_tart swimming sharp_knife thunder
dislikes cold_tea wet_floors
fears a_debt_called_in_before_it_can_be_paid a_broken_axle_far_from_town
hopes a_debt_paid_and_never_spoken_of a_new_cart_with_iron_tyres
topics work +0.4 family +0.3 travel +0.3 food +0.2 pastimes +0.2 weather +0.2 festival -0.4 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=gruff gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hauls a cart up and down the south road and has a firm opinion about everybody's grandmother: quick to bristle, proud of a sharp knife and a straight load, warm under the scowl, and close as a shut box about money owed.

words
oath! = Shafts and axles | By wheel and rut | Hub and spoke
saying! = Every wolf's their gran over again | Show me the gran and I'll tell you the pup | A gran's word outlasts a cart
cart = the cart | my old cart
shafts = the shafts | the cart-shafts
ruts = the ruts | ruts to the axle
road = the south road | the long road down
plumtart = plum tart | a wedge of plum tart, still warm
swim = a swim in the brook pool | a cold dip, frost or no frost
knife = my good knife | a blade you could shave with
grannies = everybody's gran | the grannies of this town
load = the load | my load
stewed = tea left to go cold | a cup gone cold on the tailboard
mud = the mud | mud to the hocks
boards = wet boards | a floor tracked in mud
axle = the axle | my back axle
ford = the ford | the ford at the second milestone
tailboard = the tailboard | my tailboard
pool = the brook pool | the pool below the mill
thunder = thunder | a good crack of thunder

any
opinion @1 road for 1 [self.job=carter] : #road.capitalize#'s what feeds me. Folk who moan about it have never pulled on it.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I haul their goods for a pittance and they sell them for a fortune. My #gran# had a word for that.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've hauled for the Houses since I could lift #shafts#, and not one has shown me a face. Their grans would be ashamed.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : New folk take what little work's going. I'd like to meet their grans before I trust them.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Racket and puddles of #ale#, and tears in the lane before midnight. I'll stay in.
opinion @1 times against 1 [world.times=hard|lean] : Every week pulls heavier, and the hill never looks down to see it. #bad.capitalize#.

grown
scene ruts_deep
when topic=work|travel self.job=carter self.working=yes
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #ruts.capitalize# on the south road. I near lost a wheel at the ford. | Pulled #cart# through #mud# from the second milestone. My shoulders are #tired#. | Nobody's mended the bridge boards in a year. I take it at a crawl, every time.
b[job=carter] #cart : That ford's the worst stretch. | Same here, both shoulders. | They never mend anything.
b : That sounds hard going. | Rest them, then. | Somebody ought to see to it.
a@cart : It is. You'd know. Mind the left bank; it's soft. | #bc_it_is# We'll be bent double by forty, the pair of us. | Never. Not while the likes of us keep getting across.
a : Hard going's the job. I'd not swap it, mind. | I'll rest when #load#'s off. Not before. | Somebody ought. Nobody will. #oath.capitalize#.

scene gran_judge
when topic=smalltalk|family
does give.opinion / disagree / insist
a : I can tell you all about a wolf from their gran. #saying.capitalize#. | Folk laugh, but look at any family on this street. Same gran, same temper, every one. | My #gran# could read a stranger at forty paces. I've the knack too, near enough.
b : That's a big claim. | Not every family. | What does your gran say about me, then?
a : Big or not, it's true. Go and look at your own #gran# and tell me different. | Every one I've met. Show me the gran and I'll show you the pup. | I'd not know your #gran#. But I'd wager she'd want you to stand up straight.

scene gran_tart
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #plumtart.capitalize#. Nothing beats it, and my #gran# made it best. | I had a slice of plum tart at the inn. Good. Not my #gran#'s, but good. | Every gran in the valley thinks hers is the best tart. Only one of them was right.
b : Lucky you. | High praise, from you. | And that was yours, I suppose?
a : Lucky's the word. I'd walk to #ford# and back for a wedge. | It's as high as I go. My gran's was higher. | Mine. Ask anybody who's still alive to remember, #oath#.

scene cold_dip
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I had #swim# this morning. Ice at the edges. Best thing for a stiff back. | I swim in the brook pool most days, cold or not. Folk think I'm #daft#. | There's nothing a cold swim won't wash out of you. #mud.capitalize#, temper, the lot.
b : In this weather? | You are a bit daft. | Even temper?
a : In any weather. The water doesn't care, and nor do I. | Maybe. My back's not stiff, and theirs is. | Most of it. I come out shouting, but I come out calm.

scene sharp_blade
when topic=smalltalk|work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : See this? #knife.capitalize#. I could split a hair with it. | A carter wants three things: a sound axle, a dry tarp, and a sharp knife. | I sharpen #knife# every night before I sleep. A blunt blade's a danger.
b : What do you cut, mostly? | Why a knife? | Every night?
a : Rope, mostly. When #load# shifts you've no time to pick at a knot. | Rope. A tangled load on a hill, you cut it or it cuts you. | Every night. My #grandad# did the same and never lost a finger.

scene storm_under
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hark at #thunder#. I love it, so long as I'm under something. | I sat out a storm under a hay wagon once. Best night's sleep of my life. | #thunder.capitalize# rolling round the hills. I'd rather that than the drizzle.
b : Not afraid of it? | Under a wagon? | It's loud, though.
a : Of a noise? Not me. Of being out in it, aye, I'm no fool. | Dry as a nut, with the rain drumming on the boards over me. | Loud's honest. It says what it means, like a #good# gran.

scene rain_soup
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=oakhaven
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# off every leaf, and #road# turns to soup by noon. | Rain again. Tomorrow #road# will be #mud# to the knees. | It's raining. Now watch every wolf in the house tramp it over #boards#.
b : It'll dry out. | Leave it a day. | Wipe your feet, folk.
a : It'll dry when it likes, and not before. #bad.capitalize#. | I can't. I've somewhere to be, and a promise is a promise. | Tell them. They'll not listen to me. My #gran# would've had them scrubbing.

scene tea_gone_cold
when topic=smalltalk|food
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : I set my cup on a post to tie a rope, and when I came back it was #stewed#. | Nothing worse than #stewed#. I'd sooner drink from a ditch. | My #gran# never let tea go cold in her life. She drank it scalding, every cup.
b : Drink it quicker. | A ditch, though? | Scalding?
a : I'd like to see you tie a knot one-pawed with a cup in the other. | A ditch is cold on purpose. Tea isn't. That's the difference. | Scalding. She said a cool cup was a sign of a lazy pot.

scene floor_mud
when topic=home pair.band=housemates
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody's walked the whole lane across the floor again. #boards.capitalize# from door to hearth. | #oath.capitalize#, I scrubbed that floor last night. Look at it. | Wipe your feet at the step. My #gran# had a mat, and so do we.
b : Wasn't me. | You'll scrub it again. | It's only mud.
a : It never is, in this house. Somebody's boots are lying. | I will. And I'll grumble every stroke, #oath#. | Only #mud#, and I'm the one who slips on it.

scene late_defence
when topic=caravan|prices world.wagons=late self.job=carter
does insist / concede / assess
a : Don't look at me. I'm on time; it's #road# that's late. | Folk ask me where their goods are like I've eaten them. I've not. | The wagons from down #road# are late. Not me. I'm here.
b : Nobody's blaming you. | Somebody must know. | Glad somebody is.
a : Folk are, with their eyes. I know the look. My #gran# had it. | The road knows. It doesn't say. | Somebody has to be. I'll not have it said I wasn't.

scene road_robbed
when topic=caravan|bandits world.wagons=raided self.job=carter
does tell.worry / sympathise / assess
a : A wagon robbed on #road#. That could've been my cart. | They've been at the wagons again. I'll take #knife# and go by daylight. | Robbed, on my road. #bandits.capitalize#, and nobody doing a thing about it.
b : Go careful. | Daylight's wise. | It's a hard thing.
a : I'll go careful. I'll still go. I've a living to earn. | It is. My #grandad# went by night and came home with no boots. | It is. I'd like five minutes with them, #oath#.

scene debt_quiet
when topic=dreams|prices self.owes=yes
does tell.worry / sympathise / assess
a : I owe somebody. I'll not say who, and don't ask. | A sum's owed down in the city. I'll pay it; I always pay. | Every copper I earn, a bit goes to a debt nobody here knows about.
b : Heavy thing to haul about. | You will. | Keep it to yourself, then.
a : It is. I'll carry it to the end of #road# and set it down. | I will. My #gran# never owed a copper she didn't pay. | I mean to. That's the last I'll say on it.

scene faceless_houses
when topic=times|smalltalk self.job=carter
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've hauled for the Houses my whole life and never seen a face. Not one. | The Houses own half of what's on #cart#, and they've never bought me a cup. | Up the hill they eat off silver. Down here I eat off #tailboard#.
b : That's how it is. | They're not the drinking sort. | Fair point.
a : That's how it is, and I'll not pretend it's right. | They're not the thanking sort, either. | It's the only point I've got. #oath.capitalize#.

scene hard_week
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.job=carter
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Lean times. Folk send for half #load# and pay for a third of it. | A loaf costs what a whole day's pull did last year. I've done the sums. | Each week pulls harder. The hill doesn't see, and the lane doesn't say.
b : It's hard all round. | That's bad. | I'd say it.
a : It is. Grumbling never lightened #cart#, but I'll do it anyway. | #bad.capitalize#. My #gran# would've made soup of a boot and called it supper. | Then say it louder than me. I've a cart to pull.

scene feast_noise
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / disagree / assess
a : A feast. All noise, spilt ale, and somebody weeping in the lane by dark. | I'll stay in. Somebody has to mind the house while the rest of you get #drunk#. | Every gran in town will be out telling the young 'uns how it was done right.
b : It's only once a year. | Come out for one. | They're not wrong, maybe.
a : Once a year is plenty. | One. One cup, and then home. And I'll not dance. | They're not wrong. That's what makes it so tiresome.

scene new_faces_wary
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Another new face. They'll want the work, and there's not enough as it is. | A newcomer on #road# this morning. I asked who their gran was. They didn't know. | New folk. I'll be civil. I'll not be hasty.
b : They need work too. | Didn't know their own gran? | That's fair.
a : They do. I'd just like it to be somebody else's work they take. | Didn't know. What's a wolf with no gran? Lost, that's what. | Civil and slow. That's how my #gran# met every stranger.

scene old_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I go back further than either of us will admit. | I'd haul anything for #self.friend#, and not ask what's in it. | #self.friend# is the one I'd trust with #knife#. That's saying something.
b : That's a long time. | That's trust. | It is.
a : Long enough to know the worst and stay. | It is. I don't give it out by the cartload. | It is. I'd not lend #knife# to my own gran.

scene dawn_shafts
when topic=day|work here.time=dawn self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Up before light, #shafts# in my paws, and #road# ahead of me. | I check my axle at dawn, every day. A creak at the gate's a break at #ford#. | First light. I like to be past the wall before the town's awake.
b : Early start. | Every day? | Why the hurry?
a : Early's the only start a carter gets. | Every day. My #grandad# lost a load to an axle he didn't check. | No hurry. I just like the road to myself, #oath#.

scene chapel_short
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Before #road# I ask the Bright One to keep me whole, and I give thanks when I'm home. | My #gran# went to chapel every Restday of her life. I go when I can. | The Bright One sees #road#. That's enough for me.
b : That's most of us. | When's that, then? | Fair enough.
a : Most of us that work for a living. | Not as often as she'd like. She'd tell me so, too. | Fair or not, it's what I've got.

story gran_and_miller [topic=memories|family self.age>=25]
  : My #gran# once beat the miller at arm-wrestling, on a bet, at the summer fair.
  : He was twice her size. She said it was all in the wrist and the stare. Mostly the stare.
  ask : Have you a gran who'd do a thing like that?
  b[old] : I am that gran, near enough.
  b : Not quite like that. Mine baked.
  : #saying.capitalize#. That's why I'll not back down from anybody, #oath#.

story walked_the_load [topic=work|memories self.job=carter self.age>=25]
  : One winter #road# was shut with snow, and the town was out of salt.
  : I carried it up on my back from #ford#, two sacks at a time, eleven trips.
  b : All on your back? How long did that take?
  : Three days. My back's never forgiven me. The town had salt for the feast, though.

story pool_dare [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=20]
  : As a #child# I was dared by a bigger pup into the brook pool in midwinter.
  : I went in, and I came out, and I've gone in every winter since.
  ask : Would you have taken the dare?
  b : Not in midwinter. Not for anything.
  b[old] : Once. When I was young enough to be daft.
  : That pup never took a dare of mine back. I asked. I still ask.

line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're on the road; get to the side of it. | #greet#. New to me, you are. Your gran I'd likely know.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=carter] : #greet#. Mind the wheels. | #greet#. Step clear; this load's heavy.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early for you. Not for me. | #greet#. I'm off down #road# shortly.
line @4 greet [pair.band=friends] : #greet#. There you are. | #greet#. Sit on the tailboard, if you like.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : #greet#. Eat something; you look thin. | You. #greet#. Come here.
line @1 again.open : You again. Twice in a day. | #welcome_back#. I'd not gone far.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, and the same.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family|housemates] : #greet#. Wipe your feet. | And you. #greet#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=carter] : #greet#. I'm loading; be quick. | #greet#. Mind the shafts.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep to the road. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep left at the ford.
line @1 react.news : #oath.capitalize#. Is that right. | Well. I'll hear the rest on #road#.
line @1 react.news.new : #marvel#. First I've heard. | #surprise#. Nobody told me.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Heard it at the ford. | I'd heard. Carters hear everything first.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll believe it when somebody's gran says it. | Twice-heard I'll credit. Once is wind.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a hard thing. | #oath.capitalize#. I'm sorry for it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Good. | #good.capitalize#. Their gran will be proud.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Back's stiff. It always is. | Well enough. Grumbling, mostly.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. A load to get down before dark. | #busy.capitalize#. Ask me at the ford.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down a minute. | That's #bad#. I'm sorry.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. Not today. The load's promised and I'll not break it. | I can't, not this week. I've hauls booked to the end of it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | Then I'll ask somebody else, and no hard feelings.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll not forget it. | #thanks#. Good of you.
line @1 preclose : Well. #cart.capitalize# won't load itself. | #preclose#. I've a knife to sharpen.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. #farewell#. | Off you go. Mind the ruts.
line @1 ack : Hm. | #ack#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. #bandits.capitalize# on the road. Keep off it after dark. | Stay off #road# after dark. I'm staying off it.
rule @carter_cry
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind your backs! Cart coming through. | Step aside. #load.capitalize#'s heavy and I'll not stop on a hill.

rule @axle_creak
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That axle's talking. I don't like what it's saying. | #ruts.capitalize#, every yard of it. #oath.capitalize#.

rule @thunder_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hark at that. Grand. | #thunder.capitalize#. Now that's a noise.

rule @wet_floor_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe your feet! Every one of you! | Look at #boards#. Just look at it.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. You're not from here. Who's your gran, then? | #greet#. Out with it; I've a load waiting.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I've a minute. What is it?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Say your piece and step off. I've a sharp knife and a short temper.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : I haul for the town, up and down #road#. Salt, meal, nails, whatever's promised. | I'm the #self.trade_words#. If it comes up #road#, likely I pulled it.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work. Hard, and without complaint. Mostly. | This and that, and my back aches from all of it.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. Heard it at #ford#.
dlg @2 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing on #road# but ruts.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry talk. I carry salt.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep to the side of the road. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
graft resident.hub
choice People say you know everybody's grandmother. -> grans
node grans
say Know them or not, I've an opinion. A wolf's their #gran# over again: temper, walk, the lot. Show me yours and I'll tell you about you.
mood calm
free
choice What was your own like? -> grans_own
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node grans_own
say Fierce. Baked the best plum tart in the valley and beat the miller at arm-wrestling. I've her temper and none of her baking.
choice She sounds a fine one. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
